{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Summary\n\nFound by the Step 7 (Axis 1 construct) sibling sweep while fixing `satiated-activated-aardwolf` (5524-e353-2e2d-4dbe). Same detect-only drift class as `CONFIG_PATHS`, but on the gerrit deploy-key materializer, which was overlooked when `materialize-g2p-config.sh` was added to `CONFIG_PATHS`.\n\n`infra/gerrit/materialize-deploy-key.sh` is an SSM-to-file materializer (it puts the replication deploy key into the gerrit user's dir), a direct sibling of `infra/gerrit/materialize-g2p-config.sh`. `materialize-g2p-config.sh` IS enumerated in `CONFIG_PATHS` (detect-only, `reason=config_manual`); `materialize-deploy-key.sh` is in **no** manifest. So a merged change to the deploy-key materializer rsyncs to `/opt/rebar` and silently does nothing — the same drift class `CONFIG_PATHS` detect-only was created to make visible.\n\n## Class-level plan (PRIMARY ticket for the manifest-omission class)\n\nThis ticket is the primary for a ONE class-level change fixing both confirmed instances of the class \"an infra SOURCE that affects the running environment is absent from every path manifest in `infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh`, so a merged change to it drifts silently\". The change touches ONLY `infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh` (two manifest additions) plus the new/extended regression tests. Sibling ticket `5d4c-a25b-b612-4aca` (broke-choleric-hound) is fixed in the same change.\n\nBoth instances proven at runtime with a discriminating contrast against the sibling source that IS in the manifest (see RCA comments on each ticket).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] `infra/gerrit/materialize-deploy-key.sh` is enumerated in the `CONFIG_PATHS` literal in `infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh` (Instance 1, detect-only parity with `materialize-g2p-config.sh`; applying touches gerrit so no auto-reload).\n- [x] A deploy-key-materializer-only change emits `AUTODEPLOY_ERROR reason=config_manual`, asserted by a regression test extending `tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_signals_gerrit_config.py`.\n- [x] `infra/scripts/mcp-entrypoint.sh` is enumerated in the `MCP_PATHS` literal in `infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh` (Instance 2, apply-parity; ADR 0079 v1 mcp auto-apply scope).\n- [x] An mcp-entrypoint-source-only change fires the existing blue-green mcp deploy path, asserted by a regression test in `tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_mcp_bluegreen.py` (`docker compose build mcp` invoked + nginx upstream flipped).\n- [x] [non-codebase] Each regression test is shown RED before the fix and GREEN after, with mutation teeth: emptying the manifest entry returns the test to RED. (Process/run evidence — see the RED→GREEN + mutation-teeth comment on this ticket.)\n- [x] [non-codebase] `make lint` (including shellcheck) passes. (Run result — see the verification-evidence comment; also the Gerrit `Verified +1` lint+type-check job on change 2444.)\n- [x] [non-codebase] The full `tests/scripts` suite passes. (Run result — see the verification-evidence comment; also the Gerrit `Verified +1` pytest jobs on change 2444.)\n\n## Non-goals\n\n- `observability.sh` needs no change: it already counts every `AUTODEPLOY_ERROR {` marker regardless of `reason`, so the `config_manual` signal is counted for free.\n- A structural manifest-completeness guard for this class is being evaluated separately and is intentionally out of scope. Any further same-class instances found are enumerated in the final report, not filed, per the sweep-containment directive.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `CONFIG_PATHS` includes `infra/gerrit/materialize-g2p-config.sh` but NOT `infra/gerrit/materialize-deploy-key.sh`.\n- Runtime discriminating experiment: a deploy-key-materializer-only change produced NO signal; a g2p-materializer-only change produced `AUTODEPLOY_ERROR reason=config_manual`.\n- `infra/compose/Dockerfile.mcp` bakes `mcp-entrypoint.sh` into the image (`install -m 0755 ... mcp-entrypoint.sh /usr/local/bin/mcp-entrypoint.sh`; `ENTRYPOINT`), yet it is absent from `MCP_PATHS`."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788123759452208122,"uuid":"e459a19d-e2a2-476b-8540-dce20634457e"}